00:04:07.907 --> 00:04:10.220
"Why am I able to play any VR game

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.800
for countless hours without getting sick,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.270
but the moment I start driving a car,

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.420
I get motion sickness?"

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.940
In a VR people get motion sick
because there's a disconnect

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.130
from what their vision is seeing versus

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.960
what their semicircular canals

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.390
in their ears are experiencing.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.130
So that sort of disconnect can
create nausea in some people

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.340
that you can get used to.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.650
In an automobile,

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.670
because you're constantly
starting and stopping,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.130
you're having the opposite disconnect

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.500
where your semicircular canals

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.330
are experiencing a lot of
activation, a lot of stimulus,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.670
but your vision might be
looking at a still object.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.941
So that's a different disconnect

00:04:39.941 --> 00:04:41.980
on opposite ends of the spectrum,

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.270
and you can have worse
motion sickness on one end

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.103
but not the other.

00:04:45.103 --> 00:04:47.400
"Every time I wake up
much earlier than normal,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.050
like to catch a flight, I
get really bad indigestion.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.670
Is this just coincidence
or is something going on?"

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.670
There's something going on.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.900
The central nervous
system of our bodies works

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.980
on two different systems.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.370
One is the rest, repair,
and digest nervous system

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.730
that happens and gets activated

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.540
when we sleep, when we
chill, when we meditate.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.500
And then the flight or
flight response system,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.500
which is like what happens
if we see a threat.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.420
When we're sleeping, we're in rest/digest.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.520
If you don't get enough sleep,

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.680
you don't repair, you don't digest well.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.070
So when you wake up early,

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:15.410
your body has to go into
fight or flight mode.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.670
It has to kick in your adrenaline
in order to keep you awake

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.680
and allow you to function normally.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.360
And also, many people, to
combat waking up early,

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.460
drink a ton of caffeine

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.760
which stimulates acid
secretion from your stomach,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.350
which can create gastroesophageal reflux,

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.837
which is like traditional heartburn.

00:05:30.837 --> 00:05:32.860
"What's the difference between an allergy

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.010
and an intolerance?"

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.780
Such an important question here

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:38.150
because so many people say
they're allergic to things

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.170
when they're really not.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.670
And then it creates other problems.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:41.770
So many of my patients say

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.090
that they have a penicillin allergy

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.150
when they actually don't.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.810
And as a result, they
lose a set of antibiotics

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.150
that are actually quite effective

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.920
and have a low risk of side effects.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.560
An allergy is a histamine-driven response

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.790
where you actually get itchiness, hives,

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.510
and you start scratching your skin.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:57.930
There's eosinophils present.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.430
You could also have an allergic
response to anaphylaxis

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.360
where your throat starts
closing up, you have swelling

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:06.000
because histamine start
allowing the swelling of tissues

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.150
by making blood vessels more porous.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.610
Then you get cytokines

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.320
and all these inflammatory cells come,

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.400
and it becomes a big problem

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.760
'cause it closes off your airway.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.940
An intolerance is when something

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.360
just doesn't sit right with you.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.498
It causes some other
malfunction in your body.

00:06:18.498 --> 00:06:20.780
For example, if you're lactose intolerant,

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.750
it's not an allergy because
you don't get a rash,

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.940
you don't get anaphylaxis.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.350
But you do have diarrhea,

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.637
so it's an intolerance,
but not an allergy.

00:06:27.637 --> 00:06:30.100
"Why is my pubic hair so curly?"

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.340
Okay, Max, did not expect that one.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:35.160
Pubic hair is a type of
hair called terminal hair.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.520
It starts as vellus hair on
our bodies when we're babies.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.260
Vellus hair is the type of peach fuzz hair

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.060
that we actually still have on our bodies.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.070
And in certain areas due to puberty,

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.120
we start developing terminal hair changes

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.910
and it becomes deeper,
it becomes more coarse,

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:48.870
becomes more curly.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.325
In fact, pubic hair
really doesn't grow longer

00:06:51.325 --> 00:06:54.500
than six inches because
of how often it sheds

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.333
and breaks out.

00:06:55.333 --> 00:06:57.290
Also, really interesting
about pubic hair...

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.320
Never thought I would say that.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.260
But I think the reason

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.130
that it's curly is
because back in the day,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:05.470
cavemen days/cavewomen days, we had a bush

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.650
and that bush helped us
have better locking in

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.390
of our pheromones, that smell.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.920
It was actually an
aphrodisiac at this time

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.630
when we all walked
around without clothing.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.840
It was an advantage for those

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.490
who had curlier pubes to survive.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.287
Also, pubes are great
protection from friction.

00:07:24.287 --> 00:07:26.190
